# Panel 217's R3, ratified 2026-10-17 (M-readonly-lend), the ffi-pragmatist's
# prediction: defect 2062's first case, `fixedbugs-2062-a-record-holding-a-
# union-bound-partial-builds`, whose header reads the record through
# `const struct tagged *`, written with `lent` and no `@` and called from a
# `=` binding, builds and prints what that case prints. Its header is that
# case's own.

extern "fixedbugs-2062-tagged.h"
    record Tagged tag tagged partial
        kind: i32
    function tg_kind(t: Tagged lent) -> i32

function main()
    t = Tagged(kind: 2, rest: zero)
    print(tg_kind(t))
